1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,565
On Meta, the clinical-authority cut won as filmed.

2
00:00:03,565 --> 00:00:08,901
On TikTok, that same cut barely registered, and the raw, unframed 12-hour shift cut

3
00:00:08,901 --> 00:00:10,059
won there instead.

4
00:00:10,059 --> 00:00:15,010
Same product, same claims boundary, two different answers to what works here.

5
00:00:15,010 --> 00:00:17,839
Nothing ahead asks you to make anything new.

6
00:00:17,839 --> 00:00:21,246
Every ad you've already built stays exactly as it is.

7
00:00:21,246 --> 00:00:26,454
What changes is where it runs and how it's cut for that placement, because a feed

8
00:00:26,454 --> 00:00:31,469
and a For You page don't reward the same fifteen seconds for the same reasons.

9
00:00:32,019 --> 00:00:37,228
Five lectures, moving from the two biggest placements to the matrix that ties them

10
00:00:37,228 --> 00:00:42,246
together, then closing on something most people skip: how much of the placement

11
00:00:42,246 --> 00:00:47,264
decision isn't yours anymore, because the platform's own delivery AI is already

12
00:00:47,264 --> 00:00:49,360
making part of that call for you.

13
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:54,442
Before lecture one, pull the two strongest cuts out of your Section 4.6 exports,

14
00:00:54,442 --> 00:00:55,267
artifact B04.

15
00:00:55,267 --> 00:01:00,349
Those are what get tested against every placement in this section, starting with

16
00:01:00,349 --> 00:01:00,984
Meta next.
